repository-code: 'REPLACE WITH REPOSITORY URL'
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline and model reports for a five-year grazing and cover crop
  trial at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln. Soil inorganic nitrogen is fused
  with remote sensing covariates, a water-balance index and greenhouse gas flux;
  covariates are ranked by three independent methods; and a temporal holdout
  establishes the predictive limits of a short record.
keywords:
  - soil nitrogen
  - cover crops
  - rotational grazing
  - random forest
  - gaussian process regression
  - variable importance
  - model validation
